5. THE ANSWER: is a deterministic register state free? Five arms, each of which must
   prove the chip is awake before it is allowed to touch it.
================================================================================
*** Booting Zephyr OS build v4.4.0 ***

M5StickS3 Zephyr validation app

Board: m5stack_sticks3

[00:00:00.325,000] <inf> gfx: Pixel format RGB_565 (high byte first)

[00:00:00.325,000] <inf> gfx: Display ready (135x240)

[00:00:00.397,000] <inf> audio: audio_init OK (16 kHz/16-bit, amp off)

=== HW-023d: can the driver get a deterministic register state for free? ===

  the settled noise floor on this board is 81..116. an arm that reads back a

  real floor IMMEDIATELY after its writes is one the driver can afford.

  'awake after N ms' is how long the PREVIOUS arm's damage took to clear.

  D0 configure only (control)  awake after 512   ms  ->  floor=103   FREE (no settle cost)

  D1 + digital registers       awake after 512   ms  ->  floor=123   FREE (no settle cost)

  D2 + analog registers        awake after 512   ms  ->  floor=109   FREE (no settle cost)

  D3 0xFA pulse + everything   awake after 513   ms  ->  floor=1024  FREE (no settle cost)

  D4 0x00 reset + everything   awake after 4096  ms  ->  floor=0     COSTS THE SIX SECONDS

  D4 is the known-bad control: if it does NOT cost the six seconds, this

  harness is not measuring what HW-023c measured and nothing above is safe.

=== ES8311 sample-rate sweep ===

regs  : the clock registers read back off the chip over I2C

lrck  : the frame clock MEASURED against the kernel cycle counter,

        which is not derived from the I2S clock

adc   : the microphone noise floor with the amplifier off. A codec

        whose clock tree did not lock cannot run its modulator and

        returns zeros or a stuck constant here

tone  : the captured level with the amplifier on. Reported, not

        asserted: this speaker couples weakly into this microphone.

        Judge the speaker by ear; the pitch rises across the sweep

        because the tone table was made for 16 kHz

